---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Contact & corrections — Biochemistrypedia" description="Found an error? Tell us and we'll fix it.">
  <article class="wrap prose-col" style="padding-top: var(--ddp-space-12)">
    <p class="eyebrow">Contact &amp; corrections</p>
    <h1>See something wrong? Tell us.</h1>

    <p>
      Some lecture slides use AI-assisted illustration, so a structure is
      occasionally drawn with a bond or an orientation wrong. Where we have caught
      one, the slide carries a caption saying exactly what is off. For geometry you
      intend to memorize, work from the live 3D molecules, which load by accession
      ID from RCSB&nbsp;PDB and PubChem. Each lesson&rsquo;s Sources &amp; Integrity
      panel lists every source it uses and who screened it.
    </p>

    <h2>Spotted a correction?</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:deppmann@gmail.com?subject=Biochemistrypedia%20correction">deppmann@gmail.com</a>
      with the lesson, the slide or section, and what looks off. A screenshot helps.
      I read every one, and a confirmed error gets fixed or the figure comes down.
    </p>

    <p class="src-meta">
      Corrections from students are how this gets better. Thank you for sending them.
    </p>

    <p><a href="/">← Back to lessons</a></p>
  </article>

  <style>
    .eyebrow {
      font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono);
      font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs);
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--ddp-color-accent);
    }
    .src-meta {
      color: var(--ddp-color-muted);
      font-size: var(--ddp-text-sm);
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
